A play command while stopped starts the context again from the top.

At the end of a context with autoplay off the player is stopped and a
plain play (SpircCommand::Play, which our control socket and a
speaker's tap send) returned without doing anything: only a Connect
load can start a context, and remotes cannot send one. Spotify's own
play button there plays the same context again from its first track;
now a plain play does the same. A stopped player with no context still
does nothing.

Applies on top of librespot-control-socket.patch and
librespot-session-loss-reconnect.patch.

